  "formulas": {
    "reward": "Each successful placement including the last is +0.001. On a terminal the bootstrap becomes zero, delta_T=0.001 - V(s_T). No separate death penalty or clear reward.",
    "raw_advantage": "delta_t=r_t+V(s[t+1])*I(nonterminal)-V(s[t]); A_t=delta_t+0.999*I(no termination or truncation)*A[t+1]. Across ordinary rollout boundary initialize A[t+1]=0, keeping V(s[t+1]) as bootstrap.",
    "value_target": "A_raw+V(s_t), fitted with 0.5*MSE; policy loss instead uses A_raw flattened over 32x256 and standardized by rollout mean/std, with clipped action ratio. Numerical sensitivities below apply to raw advantage and fixed-baseline critic target, before batch normalization.",
    "cutoff": "For d transitions ending in terminal (inclusive), a unit residual only contributes .999^(d-1). Equivalently for a residual at t+h the weight is .999^h if in the same-lane rollout. Max h=255 (256 placements including terminal); h=256 has zero direct coefficient. Physical terminal/truncation also blocks previous-episode leakage. Longer value forecasts and subsequent learning can bridge boundaries indirectly."
  },
