    "parent_receipt_sha256": "2ad025b3b72b9b7092fdf85bcb9fb44b1bdeda323bd67018c080a1034107bb6c",
    "boundaries": "T=0 at start of each run, fixed blocks per environment on its global lane placement counter. Terminal placement is inclusive, with one-based end counter T. Its contribution spans min(episode own placements, 1+((T-1) mod block_width)). A reset stops propagation across the old episode. The same 32 lanes, five completed arms, and exactly the same actions and behavior-policy changes are used at all widths.",
    "validation": "Reconstructed every terminal lane and absolute step from the immutable complete episode-end history, validated original update placement and terminal counters and per-arm 256 totals, then independently enumerated each lane state against its first future terminal and block boundaries for all widths. This measures whether a raw advantage contains a recorded terminal delta. In the historical data weights could change every 256 lane steps. Repartitioning those trajectories does not produce on-policy 512/1024-step training data or measure optimization, survival, or the size of the residual.",
